# PERFORMANCE_AUDIT_PHASE20.md

Part P-101 - Query/Index Audit + Cache-Hit-Rate Spot Check (Phase 20).
Status: IN PROGRESS - Step 1 of 3 done (data + index existence). Step 2 (EXPLAIN ANALYZE) and Step 3 (cache hit rates, conclusions) pending.

## Part A - Method and audit data (Step 1)

PostgreSQL version: 16.15 (Debian 16.15-1.pgdg13+2). Seed: `p101_seed.py` (fixed random seed 101, idempotent, ANALYZE run afterwards).
Audit rows are identifiable by username `p101_*`, business name `P101 *`, category slug `p101-*` and are removed by `p101_cleanup.py`.

| Data | Rows |
|---|---|
| BusinessProfile (8 cities, 3 countries, ~10% featured) | 300 |
| Product | 6000 |
| Post | 6000 |
| Reel | 3000 |
| Story (of which active: published and not expired) | 3000 (146) |

Business activity is skewed (some businesses have many items), created_at spread over 90 days, statuses mixed (published / pending_review / rejected), ~2-3% soft-deleted.

## Part B - Index existence vs Section 9 (Step 1)

Existence only. Whether the planner USES an index is Part C (Step 2). `FOUND-PREFIX` means an index exists whose leading columns match.

